<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">20 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 20 October, from 1740 to 2011.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/maria-theresa" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maria-theresa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1740">1740 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">286 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Maria Theresa inherits the Habsburg lands</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The death of Emperor Charles VI left his 23-year-old daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-theresa">Maria Theresa</a> ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>. She fought off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-the-great">Frederick the Great</a>'s challenge and reformed the state over a 40-year reign.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1803">1803 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">223 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The US Senate ratifies the Louisiana Purchase</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Senate approved the treaty buying <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> by 24 votes to 7. For 15 million dollars, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> gained some 828,000 square miles, roughly doubling its territory.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1827">1827 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">199 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Allied fleets destroy the Ottoman-Egyptian navy at Navarino</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British, French and Russian squadrons destroyed the Ottoman and Egyptian fleet in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-navarino">Navarino</a> Bay, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. The last major battle fought entirely by sailing ships, it secured Greek independence.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1944">1944 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">82 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US forces land on Leyte as MacArthur returns</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">American troops landed on Leyte, and General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douglas-macarthur">Douglas MacArthur</a> waded ashore to fulfil his 1942 promise to return to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>. Days later, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-leyte">Battle of Leyte</a> Gulf crippled the Japanese navy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2011">2011 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">15 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Muammar Gaddafi is captured and killed near Sirte</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Rebel fighters captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muammar-gaddafi">Muammar Gaddafi</a> near his hometown of Sirte and killed him shortly afterwards. His death ended 42 years of rule and the Libyan civil war.</p></div></li></ol>
